es in Eastern Europe.\n\nPuzzles reward careful looking: you hunt for clues, mend broken instruments, open stubborn locks and coax old mechanisms back to life. Inon Zur composed the score, recorded with a Budapest orchestra. It is a slow, atmospheric single-player adventure for patient players who like mysteries and a strong sense of place."}}